---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Methodology">
  <h1>Methodology</h1>
  <p class="lede">Evidence first. Scores are screening signals, not legal conclusions.</p>
  <h2>One source revision</h2><p>Models evaluate the same hashed policy bundle. Results from different policy revisions or jurisdiction contexts are never averaged.</p>
  <h2>Multiple models</h2><p>Every result is visible. Criterion medians produce the aggregate; score ranges, applicability conflicts, and minority critical warnings remain visible.</p>
  <h2>Eight evaluation areas</h2><p>Data collection; sharing and tracking; retention and rights; content, IP and AI; account control; payments and liability; disputes; transparency and vulnerable users.</p>
  <h2>Classification</h2><p>Offering type, sector, subcategory, monetization, audience, and data sensitivity make rankings comparable. Low-confidence classifications are not ranked.</p>
  <h2>Privacy</h2><p>The extension sends only hostnames. Click-only is the default; automatic lookup requires an explicit setting.</p>
</Base>
